From: Platina Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: imx363: replace broken HD mode with stock 2x2 timing

Use the complete four-lane clock/readout timing for a 2016x1512 full-field
2x2 mode rather than the imported 1080p mode. This is the geometry and
clock tuple of the stock Platina main sensor: binning 0x22, line 3144,
frame 2968, VT 280MHz and MIPI link 340MHz. Internal readout timing is at
0x30f4..0x30f7, not 0x31f4..0x31f7. The earlier r9 candidate's incomplete
clock/readout tuple produced a grid and cropped field; it was rejected.
Only this four-lane mode is validated on Platina; the unused two-lane
clock table is inherited and untested. Full-resolution mode is preserved.
Related upstream report: https://gitlab.com/sdm845-mainline/linux/-/merge_requests/104

--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx363.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx363.c
@@ -222,21 +222,19 @@
 	{ IMX363_REG_REQ_LINK_BIT_RATE_MBPS_L, 0 },
 };
 
